Project general instructions: 
Your task is to perfect and finalize the existing repository.
Only work on components that already exist.
Do not add new architecture, new systems, or new features.
Use the issue description as the authoritative list of what needs attention.
Every fix must result in real, functioning, production‑ready code — no placeholders, no mock logic, no partial implementations.
If a component does not actively work in real usage, it is not considered complete.
Polish, stabilize, and finalize each existing module until it meets expert‑level, production‑ready standards.
